.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * 
.         * I run a fixed effects model. I assume that political attitudes can 
> be measured through political party preference (plh0012_h). 
.         * Specifically, preference for a left-leaning party (leftVote  == 1).
.         * I run a fixed-effects model with standard errors clustered at the i
> ndividual level.
.         * The dummy variable leftVote is the dependent variable and the dummy
>  variable hadDaughter is the independent variable. 
.         * I also include year fixed effects.
. 
.         * xtset pid syear // already did this earlier to create lag variable
.         xtreg leftVote hadDaughter i.syear, fe vce(cluster pid) // deviation 
> from PAP_ birthOrder variable is not included as I only look at firstborn chi
> ldren. BirthOrder was mistakenly mentioned in the PAP. 

